WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.167 --> 00:00:02.602
-Hey there, everybody.
I'm Seth Meyers.

00:00:02.602 --> 00:00:04.603
Each night this week, we have
turned the open of our show over

00:00:04.603 --> 00:00:06.205
to "Late Night" writer
Amber Ruffin

00:00:06.205 --> 00:00:09.976
to tell personal stories of her
experiences with the police,

00:00:09.976 --> 00:00:12.144
and here's one more.

00:00:12.144 --> 00:00:15.347
-For the past three days,
we have opened "Late Night"

00:00:15.347 --> 00:00:20.120
with me telling a story
about run-ins with the cops.

00:00:20.120 --> 00:00:23.289
And tonight, I'm out of stories.

00:00:23.289 --> 00:00:24.691
Just kidding.
I have more.

00:00:24.691 --> 00:00:28.328
A few years ago, I'm in the car
with my white friend.

00:00:28.328 --> 00:00:31.430
He is a white man in a suit.

00:00:31.430 --> 00:00:33.866
He's just gotten off of work.

00:00:33.866 --> 00:00:39.205
Now, I'm in a head-to-toe
velvet outfit because I'm great.

00:00:39.205 --> 00:00:41.608
I think I was going to a party,

00:00:41.608 --> 00:00:44.844
so it was like
my favorite party outfit.

00:00:44.844 --> 00:00:47.847
I still remember that thing.
It was beautiful.

00:00:47.847 --> 00:00:52.184
It was not that late at night.

00:00:52.184 --> 00:00:54.687
So, we're at a truck stop,

00:00:54.687 --> 00:01:00.326
seeing if my friend's dad,
who is a truck driver, is there.

00:01:00.326 --> 00:01:03.696
We're driving slowly
along the semitrucks,

00:01:03.696 --> 00:01:06.799
looking
for his dad's license plate.

00:01:06.799 --> 00:01:11.337
So I can see why
we may have seemed suspicious.

00:01:11.337 --> 00:01:14.606
And a cop comes up,
and he taps on the window.

00:01:14.606 --> 00:01:16.342
And I'm like, "Frick!"

00:01:16.342 --> 00:01:18.844
I have been harassed
for doing nothing.

00:01:18.844 --> 00:01:20.646
I'm sure this guy
is going to get us.

00:01:20.646 --> 00:01:24.917
My friend rolls down the window,
and the cop is super nice.

00:01:24.917 --> 00:01:27.153
Now, I had never been stopped
by a cop

00:01:27.153 --> 00:01:29.889
while a white man was around.

00:01:29.889 --> 00:01:32.692
And the respect this cop had

00:01:32.692 --> 00:01:37.430
for this white man
in this suit, man, I --

00:01:37.430 --> 00:01:41.066
this cop wants to know
what in the world we are doing,

00:01:41.066 --> 00:01:42.802
and he asked politely.

00:01:42.802 --> 00:01:46.839
And we tell him,
and he is unsatisfied.

00:01:46.839 --> 00:01:48.374
He goes, "I stopped you

00:01:48.374 --> 00:01:52.345
because there's been
a lot of prostitution."

00:01:52.345 --> 00:01:56.582
[ Laughing ] And I go,
"Oh, I'm not a prostitute."

00:01:56.582 --> 00:02:00.719
And this cop has never believed
anything less.

00:02:00.719 --> 00:02:06.392
He looks at our I.D.s,
and he asks us more questions.

00:02:06.392 --> 00:02:10.963
And my white friend
is getting annoyed at this cop.

00:02:10.963 --> 00:02:12.365
And the cop can tell.

00:02:12.365 --> 00:02:13.666
But I'm like,

00:02:13.666 --> 00:02:16.469
"Oh, my gosh, please
just calm down and be cool."

00:02:16.469 --> 00:02:18.271
My friend says to the cop --
he goes,

00:02:18.271 --> 00:02:21.274
"You have nothing.
You have to let us go."

00:02:21.274 --> 00:02:25.978
And I'm like,
"You just got me killed!"

00:02:25.978 --> 00:02:29.715
But the cop goes...
[Sighs]

00:02:29.715 --> 00:02:34.420
"Okay, but you have to leave."

00:02:34.420 --> 00:02:35.588
[ Laughing ] Ok--
And then that was it.

00:02:35.588 --> 00:02:37.323
My friend was like,
"She's not a prostitute!"

00:02:37.323 --> 00:02:38.757
And I was like, "Oh, shut up.

00:02:38.757 --> 00:02:41.661
Hey, we're going.
Thank you. Goodbye."

00:02:41.661 --> 00:02:43.696
Y'all, the respect this cop

00:02:43.696 --> 00:02:47.400
just automatically had
for my friend --

00:02:47.400 --> 00:02:49.502
I'll never forget seeing it.

00:02:49.502 --> 00:02:51.337
So, that's it.

00:02:51.337 --> 00:02:53.205
That's my story.

00:02:53.205 --> 00:02:54.873
Alright.

00:02:54.873 --> 00:02:59.745
So, for the past 10 days,

00:02:59.745 --> 00:03:04.350
the George Floyd protests
were worldwide.

00:03:04.350 --> 00:03:07.854
Like, hundreds of thousands
of people

00:03:07.854 --> 00:03:11.558
all over the country,
all over the world,

00:03:11.558 --> 00:03:18.231
saw yet another video of a man
being murdered in cold blood

00:03:18.231 --> 00:03:20.033
and rose up.

00:03:20.033 --> 00:03:23.635
People all over the world
took to the streets

00:03:23.635 --> 00:03:26.139
because they believe that

00:03:26.139 --> 00:03:28.774
black people deserve
better treatment

00:03:28.774 --> 00:03:32.311
than we have been getting.

00:03:32.311 --> 00:03:33.879
[ Breathes sharply ]

00:03:33.879 --> 00:03:36.515
And, you know, I'm not like,
"Oh, wow, everything's over.

00:03:36.515 --> 00:03:37.850
Everything is fixed."

00:03:37.850 --> 00:03:41.787
But...y'all, I am so shocked

00:03:41.787 --> 00:03:48.727
that so many people showed up
for black people.

00:03:48.727 --> 00:03:55.601
We've been being discriminated
against for fun for years,

00:03:55.601 --> 00:04:02.308
and I didn't think
people cared or saw

00:04:02.308 --> 00:04:06.479
or they knew
and were fine with it.

00:04:06.479 --> 00:04:12.651
For whatever reason,
everyone is fed up, thank God.

00:04:12.651 --> 00:04:15.220
And last night,
Obama held a town hall,

00:04:15.220 --> 00:04:19.125
and he talked
about a comprehensive plan

00:04:19.125 --> 00:04:21.260
with real policies

00:04:21.260 --> 00:04:25.264
that can start saving lives
right now.

00:04:25.264 --> 00:04:27.233
He talked about easy things

00:04:27.233 --> 00:04:29.736
that every police force
in America

00:04:29.736 --> 00:04:32.104
can choose to do this second

00:04:32.104 --> 00:04:35.407
and start saving lives
this minute.

00:04:35.407 --> 00:04:36.742
[ Breathes sharply ]

00:04:36.742 --> 00:04:41.246
This change, if they enact it,
would be great.

00:04:41.246 --> 00:04:46.685
But please don't forget
that it cost us

00:04:46.685 --> 00:04:49.455
not only George Floyd's life,

00:04:49.455 --> 00:04:52.825
but the lives of 11 people

00:04:52.825 --> 00:04:56.161
who have been killed
during these protests,

00:04:56.161 --> 00:05:00.666
including David McAtee...

00:05:00.666 --> 00:05:03.035
Dave Patrick Underwood...

00:05:03.035 --> 00:05:04.703
Chris Beaty...

00:05:04.703 --> 00:05:06.238
Dorian Murrell...

00:05:06.238 --> 00:05:08.374
Italia Kelly...

00:05:08.374 --> 00:05:10.610
Calvin Horton Jr...

00:05:10.610 --> 00:05:12.344
Javar Harrell...

00:05:12.344 --> 00:05:14.480
Victor Cazares...

00:05:14.480 --> 00:05:16.382
Sean Monterrosa...

00:05:16.382 --> 00:05:18.117
David Dorn...

00:05:18.117 --> 00:05:21.987
and from my hometown
of Omaha, Nebraska,

00:05:21.987 --> 00:05:24.423
the brave James Scurlock.

00:05:24.423 --> 00:05:28.127
Don't let it cost more lives.

00:05:28.127 --> 00:05:30.129
Vote.

00:05:30.129 --> 00:05:31.631
[Bleep]

00:05:31.631 --> 00:05:33.533
I don't want to do it again.

00:05:33.533 --> 00:05:34.967
Vote.

00:05:34.967 --> 00:05:38.370
Call your representatives.
Unfriend racists.

00:05:38.370 --> 00:05:41.607
And most importantly,

00:05:41.607 --> 00:05:44.210
when you see something,
say something.

00:05:44.210 --> 00:05:46.378
Do something.
Get loud.

00:05:46.378 --> 00:05:49.781
Don't let people get away
with racist crap -- not anymore.

00:05:49.781 --> 00:05:51.417
It's a new day.

